sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor AD as Admin
  participant API as API
  participant DB as Postgres
  actor NU as Invitee

  AD->>API: POST /api/invitations {email, role} (requireAdmin)
  API->>DB: withTenant: user with this email in MY org? → 409 ALREADY_MEMBER
  Note right of DB: other orgs are NOT checked here, so admins can't probe which emails exist elsewhere
  API->>DB: revoke any open invitation for this email (re-invite replaces link)
  API->>API: token = 32 random bytes (base64url)
  API->>DB: INSERT invitations (token_hash = sha256(token), expires in 7 days)
  API-->>AD: 201 {invitation, inviteUrl = WEB_ORIGIN/invite/token}
  AD-->>NU: shares link (copy button, no email service)

  NU->>API: GET /api/auth/invitations/:token
  API->>DB: withSystem: open (not accepted, not revoked, not expired) by hash
  API-->>NU: {email, orgName, role} or 404 INVITATION_INVALID
  NU->>API: POST /api/auth/invitations/accept {token, name, password}
  API->>API: argon2id hash (outside the transaction)
  API->>DB: BEGIN, SELECT invitation ... FOR UPDATE OF i
  Note right of DB: row lock: accepting one link twice at once can't create two users
  API->>DB: email registered anywhere? → 409 EMAIL_TAKEN (one org per user)
  API->>DB: INSERT users (org_id, role from invitation)
  API->>DB: UPDATE invitations SET accepted_at = now()
  API->>DB: INSERT refresh_tokens, COMMIT
  API-->>NU: 201 session + refresh cookie → app home
